{"id": "EUVD-2026-80644", "enisaUuid": "c2dcfd55-b6a0-3314-9030-e6c2b12ba730", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nNFSD: Prevent client use-after-free during blocked-lock reaping\n\nA bare lock owner -- its only remaining reference a blocked lock on\nnn->blocked_locks_lru -- holds a raw pointer to its nfs4_client but\nno reference keeping the client alive. When the per-net laundromat\nreaps such a lock, freeing the nbl drops the owner reference\nheld through flc_owner, and the final nfs4_put_stateowner()\ntakes the client's cl_lock. Because the laundromat detaches the\nnbl first, __destroy_client() no longer finds it, so a concurrent\nforce_expire_client() can free the client before nfs4_put_stateowner()\nruns, dereferencing cl_lock in freed memory.\n\nPin the client with cl_rpc_users before dropping\nnn->blocked_locks_lock, and skip clients already expiring, whose\nblocked locks __destroy_client() frees while holding an owner\nreference. Take nn->client_lock outside nn->blocked_locks_lock.\nEvery other site holds nn->blocked_locks_lock as a leaf, acquiring\nno further lock, so placing nn->client_lock outside it cannot form\na lock-order cycle.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T10:33:35", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:49:32", "baseScore": 9.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0d53a47c913d0bce3b5ec35c28cbcca4d015f33d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7081224a59a0ca4edcd62c068588f4d900199a18", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cd489b03587378645fe0d20142a33f1ed60bac98", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6fedb2eaff77554ca7a0deffd2e8bc0d6e8b38b0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9026932ac8be4d0ae01db47f23619a98cc57b671"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-90036", "GHSA-j6h5-vv56-hq58"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.47, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "06d2a5bc-0eb0-3a02-a1b7-a5c39ace1d79", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.9"}, {"id": "263a6f3b-ff17-38af-89dc-9d44d7113b72", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7919d0a27f1e7cb324e023776aa1cbff00f1ee7b <9026932ac8be4d0ae01db47f23619a98cc57b671"}, {"id": "2a2667aa-144c-3b8a-acd3-6ba5341ca305", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.51"}, {"id": "33a532ea-7311-3731-a470-78810034b9fd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7919d0a27f1e7cb324e023776aa1cbff00f1ee7b <0d53a47c913d0bce3b5ec35c28cbcca4d015f33d"}, {"id": "49d424e8-1309-38d5-8b20-1b21045f9ed6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "70b01099-2400-3282-8d92-ff07061b1a27", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "70fce39c-8462-3a0e-9c46-e39fccd67164", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7919d0a27f1e7cb324e023776aa1cbff00f1ee7b <cd489b03587378645fe0d20142a33f1ed60bac98"}, {"id": "ad982541-f7f3-3aec-8aae-5344577f6fab", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "b7a62b7f-1082-35a9-96e8-6416033dd0fb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7919d0a27f1e7cb324e023776aa1cbff00f1ee7b <6fedb2eaff77554ca7a0deffd2e8bc0d6e8b38b0"}, {"id": "d2f66fbd-8d40-3135-8e1c-e7156c8c1d88", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7919d0a27f1e7cb324e023776aa1cbff00f1ee7b <7081224a59a0ca4edcd62c068588f4d900199a18"}, {"id": "f26e5c36-ea59-371a-bbfc-a1b7349274fd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "f819090d-e9f2-324e-aa23-c5b124a7f42c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "e8b941e1-7449-39d